        "question": "Which CAD software should a small architecture or engineering firm buy first?",
        "answer": "For most firms producing drawings, AutoCAD is the safe starting point because DWG is the common exchange format and the subscription includes seven industry toolsets. If your clients require building models, consider Revit instead or alongside. Count how many people will use each product weekly before deciding."
